The textures in mixins/modmenu/sprites.rs are Mod Menu's own
(src/main/resources/assets/modmenu, MIT), converted to runs of pixels by
tools/sprites.mjs. Buttons, the search box, scroll bars and tooltips are the
game's own widgets, as Mod Menu uses vanilla's.

This port rewrites Mod Menu's title screen and pause menu buttons, its mods
screen, its options screen and its strings in Rust for Horizon's native mod
API. Changes from the original: the mods are Horizon's (the native mods built
into the game and the content mods turned on, Minecraft and Horizon itself in
place of Minecraft and Java), with names, authors, licences, links, icons and
newer versions from Horizon's catalog instead of fabric.mod.json and Modrinth;
Configure opens a mod's page on Horizon's Options > Mods; there are no parent
and child mods (Horizon has none) and no drag and drop of mod files; the
Children, Java Color and translation options are kept on the options screen
but have nothing to change in Horizon. It is not affiliated with
TerraformersMC, Prospector, Mojang or Microsoft.
